# Zone 1, room 7: Coyote dash (BUILD.md s5, the twelve core tech interactions, 7: "dash off a ledge
# within coyote time keeps ground cooldown rules. Taught by a cliff"; docs/adr/0010, Dash: a dash
# within 6 frames of walking off a ledge is a ground dash, so the air dash stays in hand).
# Grey box (Phase 1), not art. 60 x 34 tiles, floor top at y 864, doors 128 u tall (y 736 to 864).
#
# The way: arrival plateau (x 0 to 384, open above), then a tunnel under a stand-in "overhang", a
# solid box 44 u over the floor (the standing body's height: a jump cannot climb, so the cliff
# asks for dashes, not height). Under it, left to right:
#   - Trench A (x 576 to 768): the safe first encounter. 32 u deep, solid floor, no hazard: a
#     ground dash from its edge crosses it (z1_07_coyote_dash, frame 58), and walking in costs one
#     jump back out (the roof leaves exactly enough room).
#   - The island (x 768 to 992), a run-up.
#   - Chasm B (x 992 to 1584, 592 u): a row of pit tiles 32 u under the floor, the far ledge's lip
#     at x 1584 (a box over the last pit tile, x 1584 to 1600; smooth, no cling). The tech: walk off the
#     edge, dash on one of the first 7 airborne frames (the coyote dash: horizontal, ground
#     cooldown, air dash untouched), air dash about 14 to 17 frames later and air jump about 24 to
#     29 frames after the first dash (on the air dash's last frames, a dash-jump) to lift from the
#     pit's lip to the ledge.
#   - The far ledge under the roof to x 1664, then open sky and the east door (x 1920).
#
# Why it is built this way, and what it is not. The dash is flat and the roof is low, so every
# route over B is made of dashes; what a coyote dash adds over a dash pressed at the edge is the
# few frames of running past it (up to 9 u a frame). Measured on a copy of B with no far side
# (tools/replay/gap_reach.gd's method; a random-restart hill climb, three seeds of 20 starts,
# over the spawn, first dash, second dash, jump and air jump ticks): the farthest route whose
# first dash is on the ground reaches 569 u past the edge, with the coyote dash 596 u; a far
# ledge 592 u away needs more than 582 (the collider is 20 u wide). In this room, with the
# second dash 11 to 23 and the jump 16 to 31 frames after the first (208 timings, both stick
# directions in the wider sweep): first dash on frames 84 to 93 (the last frame on the ground)
# crosses with none of them; on frames 94 to 100 (the first to the seventh airborne frame) one
# to six of them do. So it is the only way for every route searched, by 14 u, and a one-frame
# difference at the lip. It is NOT proven the only way: a hill climb is not a proof, and the
# Ember Toss (gap_reach.gd: a toss carries a route past a tech 2 sized gap) was only tried once
# (a throw from the edge stopped about 90 u out) and not searched. Flagged for the director:
# play it, and if anything else crosses, move the far ledge (the box at x 1584) closer to 580.
# Fixtures: tests/replay/zone1/07_*.
room zone1/07_coyote_dash
